# Whitelist .gitignore, the shape ~/.claude itself uses: `/*` ignores every
# root entry, then `!/<name>` re-includes the tracked ones. `git check-ignore -q
# .recon/` ALREADY matches here (rule `/*`), so an appended `.recon/` line would
# be redundant and RH4 must leave this file byte-identical.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/skills
!/CLAUDE.md
